<title>POLAND: PBR Q2 net falls to PLN 4.0 mln.</title>
<headline>PBR Q2 net falls to PLN 4.0 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>PBR preliminary results for the second quarter of the year ending June 30, 1997</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of zlotys unless stated)</p>
<p>						Q2 1997     Q2 1996</p>
<p>    operating profit		     6.65    vs  14.05</p>
<p>    pre-tax profit			 6.65    vs  14.05</p>
<p>    net profit			     3.99    vs   7.25</p>
<p>NOTE - Full company name is Polski Bank Rozwoju SA.</p>
<p>    revenues from securities	   0.04    vs   0.04</p>
<p>    interest and similar revenues   58.52    vs  52.95</p>
<p>    interest and similar costs	42.51    vs  32.65</p>
<p>@</p>
<p>    revenues from commission	   5.81    vs   3.44</p>
<p>    costs of commission		  0.81    vs   1.01</p>
<p>    income tax			     2.66    vs   6.81</p>
<p>    other taxes			    0.00    vs   0.00</p>
<p>    extraordinary profit		 0.00    vs   0.01</p>
<p>						H1 1997     H1 1996</p>
<p>    operating profit		    20.89    vs  29.21</p>
<p>    pre-tax profit			20.89    vs  29.24</p>
<p>    net profit			    12.10    vs  16.00</p>
<p>    revenues from securities	   0.04    vs   0.07</p>
<p>    interest and similar revenues  110.11    vs 102.09</p>
<p>    interest and similar costs	79.84    vs  64.03</p>
<p>@</p>
<p>    revenues from commission	  13.89    vs   6.67</p>
<p>    costs of commission		  1.01    vs   1.89</p>
<p>    income tax			     8.79    vs  13.24</p>
<p>    other taxes			    0.00    vs   0.00</p>
<p>    extraordinary profit		 0.00    vs   0.02</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
